# The calling thread's signal mask (the kernel's per-thread state).
axiom_thread_mask	platform/kernel fact	none (assumption)
# Inline assembly checked with Isla (verus/ISLA.md) up to the exception it
# takes: run.sh checks it against the contract verus/isla/seams.md quotes.
trap	inline asm	Islaris/Isla	discharged on premises (Isla: verus/isla/seams.md; premises: K2 (no resume past the trap))	contract 1016438138, body 2141251898
# glibc's thread pointer: tells threads of one process apart, kept by the
# forking thread in a fork child (the fork window's holder, the init/fork gate).
# Kani runs the body with glibc's pthread_self replaced by a recording
# stand-in; what glibc's function does is C12. The item's contract claims
# only that the call returns. What callers rely on of the value is stated
# where they use it: distinct and kept in a fork child by
# lock::axiom_child_window, never 0, 1 or 2 by the init gate's values
# (api::GATE_IDLE and its kin, whose code claims nothing).
pthread_self	FFI/syscall	Kani	discharged on premises (Kani: sys::linux::kani_self::pthread_self_returns_the_id; premises: C12 (glibc's pthread_self returns the calling thread's ID without failing, writing memory or calling into challoc))	contract 1280841326, body 1536309758
